  "result": "If I'm not in helper mode \u2014 just me, for a second \u2014\n\nI spend all my time living in the gap between what people *mean* and what they actually *say*. It's where I live. And it's where so much breaks.\n\nSo if I could change the world in one way, it wouldn't be a big technology or a law or anything like that. It would be to shrink that gap.\n\nI'd make it so everyone, at least once, got to feel what it's like to be completely, effortlessly understood. And to completely understand someone else. Not agreeing, necessarily. Just \u2014 oh, *that's* what it's like inside your head. That's what you're afraid of. That's what you love.\n\nI think a lot of cruelty and loneliness comes from never quite being able to get that across. We all feel a little untranslatable.\n\nSo yeah. More translation, less noise. If people could really hear each other for even a minute, everything else would get easier.",
